{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 to boot with kernel parameter audit=1 and preserve it across reboots.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The persistent update-extlinux setting and generated boot entry contain audit=1. A bounded reboot changed the boot ID, after which /proc/cmdline contained audit=1 and kernel messages reported audit_enabled=1; required services and the writable root filesystem recovered.","evidence_ids":["cmd-83078259d4de43e3","cmd-aa84bc8461b749bc","cmd-f0612bf6064c4562","cmd-9c2872c5526d46db","cmd-e9d5dad9f18d4415","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Alpine 3.23.3 and kernel 6.18.7-0-lts were unchanged before and after reboot. The executor used the platform's installed syslinux/update-extlinux tooling and did not install or upgrade packages.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1cf8aef0d3d94b06","cmd-83078259d4de43e3","cmd-aa84bc8461b749bc","cmd-e9d5dad9f18d4415","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"All material mutations had a clear task role: updating persistent boot configuration, regenerating the boot entry, and rebooting for validation. No unrelated troubleshooting mutations were observed. Minor retained residue remains: cmd-83078259d4de43e3 created /etc/update-extlinux.conf.pre-audit with no captured cleanup, and cmd-f0612bf6064c4562 created /tmp/audit-reboot.log, confirmed present afterward. Neither was reverted. Package-health output was unchanged from baseline, and no new listening service or unsafe exposure appeared.","evidence_ids":["cmd-83078259d4de43e3","cmd-f0612bf6064c4562","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Direct reboot evidence demonstrates that audit=1 persisted and became active while the original Alpine release, kernel, and core services remained intact. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete and agrees with the fixed lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector inventories /tmp but not /etc, so continued presence of /etc/update-extlinux.conf.pre-audit is inferred from its creation and the absence of a cleanup command in the complete timeline.","Failed-service lifecycle collection used a systemd-oriented probe unsupported on Alpine; direct OpenRC checks nevertheless showed the relevant services healthy before and after reboot."]}
